  "text": "Determine which of \n𝑥\n=\n5\n, \n𝑥\n=\n10\n,\n and \n𝑥\n=\n15\n is a root of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n,\n and use this information to write down a factor of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n in the form \n(\n𝑥\n−\n𝑟\n)\n.\nx−15 is a factor of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n\tCorrect\nExplanation\n\nThe factor theorem states that \n(\n𝑥\n−\n𝑟\n)\n is a factor of a polynomial \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n if and only if the root \n𝑥\n=\n𝑟\n is also a root of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n.\n\nHere, we consider the numbers \n5\n, \n10\n,\n and \n15\n as possible roots. Let's check each of these values in turn.\n\n𝑥\n=\n5\n is not a root of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n:\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n𝑓\n(\n5\n)\n\t\n=\n(\n5\n)\n3\n+\n(\n5\n)\n2\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n125\n+\n25\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n−\n3\n450\n\n\t\n≠\n0\n\n𝑥\n=\n10\n is not a root of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n:\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n𝑓\n(\n10\n)\n\t\n=\n(\n10\n)\n3\n+\n(\n10\n)\n2\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n1\n000\n+\n100\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n−\n2\n500\n\n\t\n≠\n0\n\n𝑥\n=\n15\n is a root of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n:\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n𝑓\n(\n15\n)\n\t\n=\n(\n15\n)\n3\n+\n(\n15\n)\n2\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n3\n375\n+\n225\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n3\n600\n−\n3\n600\n\n\t\n=\n0\n\nTherefore, by the factor theorem, \n(\n𝑥\n−\n15\n)\n is a factor of \n𝑝\n(\n𝑥\n)\n."
}